Count Your Pulse — Pixel Countdown Science demo · credits & licences

ORIGINAL (made for this film, by code in this folder)
- All pixel art: the heart character, ribcage, pulse gauge, cell ground, ECG plane (hero.js, scene.js, main.js).
- Captions, counter and gauge digits (font.js, scene.js).
- Music and sound effects: synthesised with numpy (mix.py); the end melody is original.

CODE ADAPTED FROM LEMO-OPUSCAR (MIT licence, github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar)
- px.js (indexed framebuffer, Bayer dither, LUTs) and the 5×7 glyph table in font.js,
  adapted from styles/pixel-rpg/demo. Sound helpers from core/audio/sfx.py (used via LIB).

PALETTE
- ENDESGA 32 by ENDESGA (public palette, lospec.com/palette-list/endesga-32), plus custom ground/yellow/ECG tones.

FACTS (captions)
- Resting adult heart rate 60–100 bpm (American Heart Association). 15-second count × 4 = beats per minute.
- Resting stroke volume ≈ 70 mL per beat (standard physiology texts).
- Near-maximal heart rate during sprinting for a young adult ≈ 180–200 bpm (≈ 220 − age, a rough estimate).

No third-party images, fonts, samples or recordings are used. No voice.
